SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ffggeettcc(), ggeettcc(), and ggeettcchhaarr() functions conform to ISO/IEC 9899:1990
     (“ISO C90”).  The ggeettcc__uunnlloocckkeedd() and ggeettcchhaarr__uunnlloocckkeedd() functions con‐
     form to IEEE Std 1003.1-2001 (“POSIX.1”).

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ggeettcc() and ggeettww() functions appeared in a similar form in Version 1
     AT&T UNIX; and were integrated into stdio in Version 7 AT&T UNIX;
     ggeettcchhaarr() in Version 4 AT&T UNIX; and ffggeettcc() in Version 7 AT&T UNIX.

BBUUGGSS
     Since EOF is a valid integer value, feof(3) and ferror(3) must be used to
     check for failure after calling ggeettww().  The size and byte order of an
     _i_n_t varies from one machine to another, and ggeettww() is not recommended for
     portable applications.

